§ `s 2014(f)(1) Averaging`

-- src:359 | Household income for those households that, by contract for other than an hourly or piecework basis or by self-employment, derive their annual income in a period of time shorter than one year shall be calculated by averaging such income over a twelve-month period.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(A), first sentence (src:359)
GIVEN `the household derives its annual income, by contract for other than an hourly or piecework basis or by self-employment, in a period of time shorter than one year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(1)(A) the household income is averaged over a twelve-month period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household derives its annual income, by contract for other than an hourly or piecework basis or by self-employment, in a period of time shorter than one year`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be calculated by averaging such income over a twelve-month period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "those households that" derive their annual income in a period shorter than one year

-- src:359 | (A) Household income for those households that, by contract for other than an hourly or piecework basis or by self-employment, derive their annual income in a period of time shorter than one year shall be calculated by averaging such income over a twelve-month period. Notwithstanding the preceding sentence, household income resulting from the self-employment of a member in a farming operation, who derives income from such farming operation and who has irregular expenses to produce such income, may, at the option of the household, be calculated by averaging such income and expenses over a 12-month period. Notwithstanding the first sentence, if the averaged amount does not accurately reflect the household’s actual monthly circumstances because the household has experienced a substantial increase or decrease in business earnings, the State agency shall calculate the self-employment income based on anticipated earnings.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(A), first sentence, the averaging (src:359)
GIVEN `the annual income derived in the period shorter than one year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(f)(1)(A) the monthly income when averaged over a twelve-month period` MEANS
    `the annual income derived in the period shorter than one year, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 12

-- src:359 | Notwithstanding the preceding sentence, household income resulting from the self-employment of a member in a farming operation, who derives income from such farming operation and who has irregular expenses to produce such income, may, at the option of the household, be calculated by averaging such income and expenses over a 12-month period.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(A), second sentence (src:359)
GIVEN `the household income results from the self-employment of a member in a farming operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member derives income from the farming operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has irregular expenses to produce the income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household chooses to have the income and expenses averaged over a 12-month period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(1)(A) the farming income and expenses may be averaged over a 12-month period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the household income results from the self-employment of a member in a farming operation` AND `the member derives income from the farming operation` AND `the member has irregular expenses to produce the income`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for income from "the self-employment of a member in a farming operation, who derives income from such farming operation and who has irregular expenses to produce such income"
        IF `the household chooses to have the income and expenses averaged over a 12-month period`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "may, at the option of the household, be calculated by averaging such income and expenses over a 12-month period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the household has the option and has not taken it, and the sentence does not say what follows

-- src:359 | averaging such income and expenses over a 12-month period.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(A), second sentence, the averaging of the expenses (src:359)
GIVEN `the annual expenses to produce the farming income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(f)(1)(A) the monthly expenses when averaged over a 12-month period` MEANS
    `the annual expenses to produce the farming income, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 12

-- src:359 | Notwithstanding the first sentence, if the averaged amount does not accurately reflect the household’s actual monthly circumstances because the household has experienced a substantial increase or decrease in business earnings, the State agency shall calculate the self-employment income based on anticipated earnings.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(A), third sentence (src:359)
GIVEN `the averaged amount does not accurately reflect the household's actual monthly circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household has experienced a substantial increase or decrease in business earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(1)(A) the State agency must calculate the self-employment income on anticipated earnings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the averaged amount does not accurately reflect the household's actual monthly circumstances` AND `the household has experienced a substantial increase or decrease in business earnings`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the State agency shall calculate the self-employment income based on anticipated earnings"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the averaged amount does not accurately reflect the household's actual monthly circumstances because the household has experienced a substantial increase or decrease in business earnings" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:360 | Household income for those households that receive nonexcluded income of the type described in subsection (d)(3) of this section shall be calculated by averaging such income over the period for which it is received.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(B) (src:360)
GIVEN `the household receives nonexcluded income of the type described in subsection (d)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(1)(B) the household income is averaged over the period for which it is received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household receives nonexcluded income of the type described in subsection (d)(3)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be calculated by averaging such income over the period for which it is received"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is for "those households that receive nonexcluded income of the type described in subsection (d)(3)"

-- src:360 | shall be calculated by averaging such income over the period for which it is received.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(B), the averaging (src:360)
GIVEN `the nonexcluded income received over the period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the period for which it is received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(f)(1)(B) the monthly income when averaged over the period for which it is received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of months in the period for which it is received` AT MOST 0
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how to average over a period of no months
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the nonexcluded income received over the period, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the number of months in the period for which it is received`)

-- src:361 | (C) Simplified determination of deductions.—
-- src:362 | (i) In general.—
-- src:363 | Except as provided in clause (ii), for the purposes of subsection (e), a State agency may elect to disregard until the next recertification of eligibility under section 2020(e)(4) of this title 1 or more types of changes in the circumstances of a household that affect the amount of deductions the household may claim under subsection (e).
-- src:364 | (ii) Changes that may not be disregarded.—
-- src:365 | Under clause (i), a State agency may not disregard—
-- src:366 | (I) any reported change of residence; or
-- src:367 | (II) under standards prescribed by the Secretary, any change in earned income.
@ref s 2014(f)(1)(C), simplified determination of deductions (src:361-367)
GIVEN `the change in the circumstances of the household affects the amount of deductions the household may claim under subsection (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is a reported change of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is a change in earned income that the standards prescribed by the Secretary do not allow to be disregarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(1)(C) the State agency may disregard the change until the next recertification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the change is a reported change of residence`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a State agency may not disregard— (I) any reported change of residence"
        IF `the change is a change in earned income that the standards prescribed by the Secretary do not allow to be disregarded`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a State agency may not disregard ... under standards prescribed by the Secretary, any change in earned income"
        IF `the change in the circumstances of the household affects the amount of deductions the household may claim under subsection (e)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a State agency may elect to disregard until the next recertification of eligibility ... 1 or more types of changes in the circumstances of a household that affect the amount of deductions"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for changes "that affect the amount of deductions the household may claim under subsection (e)"

§ `s 2014(f)(2) The basis on which income is calculated`

DECLARE `s 2014(f)(2) basis of the calculation` IS ONE OF
    `s 2014(f)(3)(A) prospective basis`
    `s 2014(f)(3)(B) retrospective basis`
    `s 2014(f)(2)(B) the income and circumstances of the first or second month`
    `s 2014(f)(2) basis not covered by this text`

-- src:369 | (A) Except as provided in subparagraphs (B), (C), and (D), households shall have their incomes calculated on a prospective basis, as provided in paragraph (3)(A), or, at the option of the State agency, on a retrospective basis, as provided in paragraph (3)(B).
-- src:370 | (B) In the case of the first month, or at the option of the State, the first and second months, during a continuous period in which a household is certified, the State agency shall determine eligibility and the amount of benefits on the basis of the household’s income and other relevant circumstances in such first or second month.
-- src:371 | (C) Households specified in clauses (i), (ii), and (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A) of this title shall have their income calculated on a prospective basis, as provided in paragraph (3)(A).
-- src:372 | (D) Except as provided in subparagraph (B), households required to submit monthly reports of their income and household circumstances under section 2015(c)(1) of this title shall have their income calculated on a retrospective basis, as provided in paragraph (3)(B).
@ref s 2014(f)(2), the four subparagraphs together (src:369-372)
GIVEN `this is the first month of a continuous period in which the household is certified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this is the second month of a continuous period in which the household is certified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State has opted to apply subparagraph (B) to the first and second months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(c)(1)(A) the household is specified in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(c)(1) the household is required to submit monthly reports of its income and household circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has opted for the retrospective basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2014(f)(2) basis of the calculation`
`s 2014(f)(2) the basis on which the household's income is calculated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`this is the first month of a continuous period in which the household is certified` OR (`this is the second month of a continuous period in which the household is certified` AND `the State has opted to apply subparagraph (B) to the first and second months`))
           AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(c)(1)(A) the household is specified in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)`
            THEN `s 2014(f)(2)(B) the income and circumstances of the first or second month`
        IF `this is the first month of a continuous period in which the household is certified` OR (`this is the second month of a continuous period in which the household is certified` AND `the State has opted to apply subparagraph (B) to the first and second months`)
            THEN `s 2014(f)(2) basis not covered by this text`  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subparagraphs (A) and (D) each yield to (B) in their own words, but subparagraph (C) does not, and the household is in (C) or the answer for (C) was not supplied
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(c)(1)(A) the household is specified in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)`
           AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(c)(1) the household is required to submit monthly reports of its income and household circumstances`
            THEN `s 2014(f)(3)(A) prospective basis`
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(c)(1)(A) the household is specified in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)`
           AND `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(c)(1) the household is required to submit monthly reports of its income and household circumstances`
            THEN `s 2014(f)(3)(B) retrospective basis`
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(c)(1)(A) the household is specified in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)`
           AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(c)(1) the household is required to submit monthly reports of its income and household circumstances`
            THEN (IF `the State agency has opted for the retrospective basis` THEN `s 2014(f)(3)(B) retrospective basis` ELSE `s 2014(f)(3)(A) prospective basis`)
        OTHERWISE `s 2014(f)(2) basis not covered by this text`  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the household is in both (C) and (D), which give opposite bases, or the answer for (C) or (D) was not supplied

§ `s 2014(f)(3) The two bases`

DECLARE `s 2014(f)(3)(A) figures taken into account` HAS
    `s 2014(f)(3)(A) the income reasonably anticipated to be received by the household during the period for which eligibility or benefits are being determined` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2014(f)(3)(A) the income received by the household during the preceding thirty days` IS A NUMBER

-- src:374 | (A) Calculation of household income on a prospective basis is the calculation of income on the basis of the income reasonably anticipated to be received by the household during the period for which eligibility or benefits are being determined. Such calculation shall be made in accordance with regulations prescribed by the Secretary which shall provide for taking into account both the income reasonably anticipated to be received by the household during the period for which eligibility or benefits are being determined and the income received by the household during the preceding thirty days.
@ref s 2014(f)(3)(A), prospective basis (src:374)
GIVEN anticipated IS A NUMBER
      `received in the preceding thirty days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 2014(f)(3)(A) figures taken into account`
`s 2014(f)(3)(A) the figures the prospective calculation takes into account` MEANS
    `s 2014(f)(3)(A) figures taken into account` WITH
        `s 2014(f)(3)(A) the income reasonably anticipated to be received by the household during the period for which eligibility or benefits are being determined` IS anticipated
        `s 2014(f)(3)(A) the income received by the household during the preceding thirty days` IS `received in the preceding thirty days`

-- src:375 | Calculation of household income on a retrospective basis is the calculation of income for the period for which eligibility or benefits are being determined on the basis of income received in a previous period.
@ref s 2014(f)(3)(B), retrospective basis (src:375)
GIVEN `the income received in a previous period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(f)(3)(B) the income calculated on a retrospective basis` MEANS
    `the income received in a previous period, in dollars`

-- src:375 | (B) Calculation of household income on a retrospective basis is the calculation of income for the period for which eligibility or benefits are being determined on the basis of income received in a previous period. Such calculation shall be made in accordance with regulations prescribed by the Secretary which may provide for the determination of eligibility on a prospective basis in some or all cases in which benefits are calculated under this paragraph. Such regulations shall provide for supplementing the initial allotments of newly applying households in those cases in which the determination of income under this paragraph causes serious hardship.
@ref s 2014(f)(3)(B), last sentence (src:375)
GIVEN `the household is newly applying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination of income on a retrospective basis causes the household serious hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(3)(B) the initial allotment must be supplemented` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is newly applying` AND `the determination of income on a retrospective basis causes the household serious hardship`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "supplementing the initial allotments of newly applying households in those cases in which the determination of income under this paragraph causes serious hardship"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the supplement is for "newly applying households in those cases in which" the determination "causes serious hardship"

§ `s 2014(f)(4) Waiver at a State agency's request`

-- src:376 | The Secretary is authorized, upon the request of a State agency, to waive any of the provisions of this subsection (except the provisions of paragraph (2)(A)) to the extent necessary to permit the State agency to calculate income for purposes of this chapter on the same basis that income is calculated under title IV–A of the Social Security Act in that State.
@ref s 2014(f)(4), waiver (src:376)
GIVEN `the State agency has requested the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is paragraph (2)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waiver is necessary to permit the State agency to calculate income for purposes of this chapter on the same basis that income is calculated under title IV-A of the Social Security Act in that State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(f)(4) the Secretary may waive the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is paragraph (2)(A)`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to waive any of the provisions of this subsection (except the provisions of paragraph (2)(A))"
        IF `the State agency has requested the waiver` AND `the waiver is necessary to permit the State agency to calculate income for purposes of this chapter on the same basis that income is calculated under title IV-A of the Social Security Act in that State`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "authorized, upon the request of a State agency, to waive any of the provisions of this subsection ... to the extent necessary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the authority is "upon the request of a State agency" and "to the extent necessary" to calculate income on the title IV-A basis
